            <section>
              <section>
                <header>An application server for PHP</header>
                <paragraph>Velocity starts Exponential once and keeps it in memory, so a request no longer pays for loading the system. Together with view caching, template compilation and a response cache it serves busy sites on modest hardware.</paragraph>
              </section>
              <section>
                <header>Familiar to run</header>
                <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">
                  <ul>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">Configuration laid out like Debian's Apache: sites, modules and snippets, each enabled with one command.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">HTTPS with automatic certificates and graceful restarts.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">Works next to PHP-FPM, so you can move one site at a time.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </paragraph>
              </section>
            </section>
          </section>
